# Agent configuration. AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .mcp.json and .claude/{settings.json,skills,hooks}
# are committed on purpose — they are project tooling. These two are per-machine and are not:
# settings.local.json holds absolute paths from whoever ran the session, and CLAUDE.local.md is
# personal preference. Committing either puts one contributor's laptop into everyone's config.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md

# Scratch git worktrees for parallel agent sessions. They are real checkouts of this
# repository, so committing one nests the tree inside itself.
.claude/worktrees/

# Codex CLI. It mirrors .claude/ — see .claude/AGENTS.md for the sync map — and it writes
# per-session state into its own directory, so the directory is ignored and only the shared
# files are re-included. The same rule as settings.local.json above, applied the other way
# round: allow-list what is shared rather than chase what is not.
.codex/*
!.codex/AGENTS.md
!.codex/config.toml
!.codex/hooks.json
!.codex/agents/
!.codex/rules/
